# MKVTOOLNIX
Nixpkgs: mkvtoolnix
Source: https://mkvtoolnix.download
Description: Set of tools to create, alter and inspect Matroska (MKV) files
Version: 85.0

## Commands

### Basics
- mkvmerge -o [output].mkv [input1].mp4 [input2].mks: create an MKV from multiple sources
- mkvinfo [file].mkv: list all tracks and elements in an MKV file
- mkvextract [file].mkv tracks [ID]:[output]: extract a specific track (audio, video, subs)

### Essentials
- mkvmerge -i [file].mkv: identify tracks and IDs in a file (quick view)
- mkvpropedit [file].mkv --edit track:a1 --set language=por: change track metadata (e.g., language) without remuxing
- mkvmerge -o [output].mkv --audio-tracks [IDs] [input].mkv: keep only specific audio tracks

### Intermediaries
- mkvmerge -o [output].mkv --default-track [ID] [input].mkv: set a specific track as the default
- mkvmerge -o [output].mkv --split size:1G [input].mkv: split an MKV into 1GB parts
- mkvpropedit [file].mkv --set title="New Title": change the global title of the MKV

### Advanceds
- mkvmerge -o [output].mkv [video].mp4 + [audio].m4a: append files (concatenate)
- mkvmerge -o [output].mkv --chapters [chapters].xml [input].mkv: add chapters to an existing MKV
- mkvextract [file].mkv attachments [ID]:[filename]: extract embedded fonts or images

### Uncommons
- mkvmerge --capabilities: list supported formats and features
- mkvinfo -v [file].mkv: verbose output including detailed structural information

## Tips
- mkvpropedit is extremely fast because it modifies the header without rewriting the entire file
- use mkvmerge -i to find the correct Track IDs before using mkvextract

## Disclaimers
- mkvmerge does not transcode video or audio; it only changes the container format (remuxing)

## Alternatives
- ffmpeg: more versatile for transcoding, but mkvtoolnix is the specialist for MKV structure

